  "geometryBasis": "The museum’s identity and connected outer shape are established by named OpenStreetMap way 491583514. Separate mapped outlines control the Green Dome, fountain, small historic tombs and the lodge’s kitchen and cells. A published architectural survey checks the 30.5 m square mausoleum core and 68 m by 84 m courtyard.",
  "sectionBasis": "Türkiye’s restoration record documents the 16 turquoise-tiled lobes of the tomb tower. The museum’s former director identifies the 18 dervish cells, the semahane and mosque, and the location of its single-balconied minaret. Qualla’s cleared exact original shows the fluted Green Dome, lead domes, single minaret and dressed stone.",
  "limitations": [
    "Model depicts the standing historic exterior. Lower roof junctions, most small window openings and the exact terrace and paving courses are approximations.",
    "The cube and cylindrical drum follow documented proportions and the native roof plan. Fine polychrome tile and inscription detail are simplified.",
    "The nearby two-minareted Selimiye Mosque is a separate landmark. The map control includes it to disambiguate the museum."
  ],
